      "message": "fix(multiaxis): state the rotaries before the first tilted feed\n\nA leaning 5-axis path left its opening moves without a pose, and the\ndump commanded zero angles only after a lean. The Fanuc angle memory\nstayed unknown, so the first tilted feed refused at a stated rotary\nrate (tilthead.mch).\n\n- stamp: when a path leans, each station before the first lean states\n  the upright Z column; a path that never leans stays silent.\n- dump: in a stream that leans, the first move that states the Z\n  column commands explicit zero angles. A stream that states no pose\n  before its first tilted feed still refuses.\n\nThe opening rapid at the clearance now carries A0 B0. The rate guard\nis unchanged.\n\nFixes #3300\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
